# tests/definitions/flat.rxtin — THE HAND-WRITTEN FLAT CONTROL.
#
# One block per block in `composed.rxtin`, same name, same cases, and a
# pattern written BY HAND with the definitions inlined. It shares no source
# with the composer: nothing here was produced by pcrec, and the patterns are
# ordinary self-contained regexes that python `re` verifies directly.
#
# WHY INLINING IS THE RIGHT CONTROL rather than a `(?(DEFINE)…)` textual
# append. The append is the thing the composer REPLACES, and it is the thing
# format_design §2.3.3 MEASURED to be wrong — it inverts a library piece's
# meaning by renumbering its backreferences. A control that reproduced the
# composer's own numbering would be a second implementation of the very rule
# under test. Inlining asks a different and simpler question — does the
# composed artifact MATCH THE SAME STRINGS — and that is what `m`/`n` assert.
#
# A subroutine call is capture-transparent, so a definition inlines as a
# NON-CAPTURING group. Every pattern below was verified against python `re`
# (2026-09-03) before it was written down.
description the flat twins of composed.rxtin, hand-written; the identity control

pattern ^(?:[a-z]+)-(?:[0-9]+)$
name pair
m "abc-42" 0 6
n "abc-"
n "-42"
n "abc-4x"

pattern ^(?:[0-9]+) (?:[a-z]+(?:\.[a-z]+)+)$
name logline
m "80 a.b" 0 6
m "80 a.b.c" 0 8
n "80 ab"
n "x a.b"

pattern ^(?:[a-z]+\.[a-z]+)$
name pairdot
m "ab.cd" 0 5
n "abcd"
n "ab."

pattern ^(\d)-(\d)\2$
name rep
m "5-77" 0 4
m "5-11" 0 4
n "5-75"
n "55-77"

# The flat twins of the three DELIVERING blocks. Each is the definition's body
# inlined at the site with its groups renamed `site_x` — addendum 4(2)'s own
# oracle rule, written out by hand here so the identity proof has something to
# compare a delivery against that pcrec did not produce.

pattern ^(?<w_word>[a-z]+)-(?:[0-9]+)$
name pairdeliv
m "abc-42" 0 6
n "abc-"
n "-42"

pattern ^(?:[0-9]+) (?<h_host>[a-z]+(?:\.[a-z]+)+)$
name logdeliv
m "80 a.b" 0 6
m "80 a.b.c" 0 8
n "80 ab"

pattern ^(?<word>[a-z]+)@(?<host>[a-z]+(?:\.[a-z]+)+)$
name flatdeliv
m "me@a.b" 0 6
n "me@ab"
